        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "70512ad4-cb3b-5320-93a7-77671350913f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jayaprakash Narayan, Binayak Sen\n- Organizations: People's Union for Civil Liberties (PUCL), People's Union for Civil Liberties and Democratic Rights (PUCLDR)\n- Awards: Bharat Ratna\n- Topics: human rights, social work\n\nFacts:\n- In 1976, Jayaprakash Narayan formed the People's Union for Civil Liberties and Democratic Rights in India as a human rights body.\n- The People's Union for Civil Liberties and Democratic Rights is referred to as the People's Union for Civil Liberties.\n- In 1999, Jayaprakash Narayan was posthumously awarded the Bharat Ratna in recognition of his social work.\n- The Bharat Ratna is the highest civilian award of the Republic of India.\n- Binayak Sen is the national Vice-President of the People's Union for Civil Liberties.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "e97df1fc-695d-54cc-be6e-d486c9d4775a",
        "text": "Page: Jayaprakash Narayan. Sentence: In 1999, he was posthumously awarded the Bharat Ratna, India's highest civilian award, in recognition of his social work.\nPage: Bharat Ratna. Sentence: The Bharat Ratna (] ; \"Jewel of India\") is the highest civilian award of the Republic of India.\nPage: People's Union for Civil Liberties. Sentence: People's Union for Civil Liberties (PUCL) is a human rights body formed in India in 1976 by socialist leader Jayaprakash Narayan, as the People's Union for Civil Liberties and Democratic Rights (PUCLDR).\nPage: Binayak Sen. Sentence: He is the national Vice-President of the People's Union for Civil Liberties (PUCL).",
